    "Starch is made in the chloroplast: glucose-1-phosphate and ATP become ADP-glucose (activated glucose) through ADP-glucose pyrophosphorylase; starch synthase joins α-(1,4) chains, and branching enzyme adds α-(1,6) branches. Starch is insoluble, so it can build up without osmotic consequences.",
    "Kanji dibuat dalam kloroplas: glukosa-1-fosfat dan ATP menjadi ADP-glukosa (glukosa teraktif) melalui ADP-glukosa pirofosforilase; kanji sintase menyambung rantai α-(1,4), dan enzim pencabangan menambah cabang α-(1,6). Kanji tidak larut, jadi ia boleh terkumpul tanpa kesan osmotik.",
